WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.433 --> 00:00:02.883
Unit five. Fitness Planning!

2
00:00:03.776 --> 00:00:07.512
Hello, everyone! I'm Doctor Visal, your school doctor.

3
00:00:07.562 --> 00:00:10.624
Hi, Doctor Visal! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:10.674 --> 00:00:14.039
Today we learn about Fitness Planning. Let's go!

5
00:00:14.923 --> 00:00:18.739
Fitness plan. Say it with me. Fitness plan!

6
00:00:22.205 --> 00:00:25.655
Cardio. Say it with me. Cardio!

7
00:00:29.202 --> 00:00:32.202
Strength. Say it with me. Strength!

8
00:00:35.658 --> 00:00:39.425
Flexibility. Say it with me. Flexibility!

9
00:00:42.979 --> 00:00:46.846
Goal-setting. Say it with me. Goal-setting!

10
00:00:50.304 --> 00:00:54.237
Consistency. Say it with me. Consistency!

11
00:00:57.725 --> 00:01:01.292
Progress. Say it with me. Progress!

12
00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:08.417
Balance. Say it with me. Balance!

13
00:01:11.918 --> 00:01:23.133
A good fitness plan includes cardio, strength, and flexibility exercises. Setting a realistic goal and staying consistent helps me see real progress. Balance between exercise and rest matters too.

14
00:01:23.183 --> 00:01:26.100
Now I understand. Thank you, Doctor Visal!

15
00:01:27.584 --> 00:01:32.606
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:32.656 --> 00:01:33.783
Strength!

17
00:01:34.492 --> 00:01:39.531
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:39.581 --> 00:01:40.731
Progress!

19
00:01:41.841 --> 00:01:48.358
Did you know? Mixing different types of exercise, not just one, helps prevent injury and keeps workouts interesting.

20
00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:50.399
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:51.781 --> 00:01:59.854
Think and answer. What would a balanced weekly fitness plan look like for you?

22
00:01:59.904 --> 00:02:01.054
Great answer!

23
00:02:02.186 --> 00:02:06.863
Great job today! Stay healthy, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:06.913 --> 00:02:09.412
Goodbye, everyone! Stay healthy!

